+- `0003-ext-bg-run.patch` - a rotated or scaled extended background (a
+  bitmap, or a 16-bit tile map) fetched each pixel through the VRAM view's
+  per-block lookup. When every 16 KB block of the bitmap, or of the map and
+  the tileset, is backed by exactly one bank and the blocks lie back to back
+  in host memory (`vram_run`, from the view's own block pointers), each pixel
+  is one load from that range; otherwise the per-pixel fetch, unchanged.
+  Mario Kart DS's lower screen in a race: engine B's worker thread 28% less
+  CPU, and the emulation thread's wait for it at line 0 from 2.3 to 0.5 ms a
+  frame (Pixel 2, 2026-11-16). Checked frame for frame against the core
+  without it: ZyperOS's mk/dsperate-extbg-check.sh (96 frames of bitmaps,
+  direct colour and tile maps in four bank layouts) and Pokemon Black frames
+  from a saved state.
